	(text "Since the LMX2582 only cannot output arbitrary frequencies independently on port A and B,\nI've decided that they will always output the same frequency (simplifies design). Therefore, \nthe filter bank selection signal will be shared between port A and B, simplifying interface. \nNote: SW_IN and SW_OUT have to be logically inverted for the design to work. It was deemed that \nit was simpler to just address two GPIOs in an inverted fashion rather then adding another inverter\npart to the BOM."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 305.816 130.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2a57370f-9032-48c9-a77a-19f24e1dde4b")
	)
	(text "Output B Switched Filter Bank of 5th order Chebychev Lowpass filters:\nUpper path: 1050 MHz cutoff\nLower path: 3000 MHz cutoff"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 270.256 78.232 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6f4aae11-3821-4188-b78f-b355c8dbffcd")
	)
	(text "Output A Switched Filter Bank of 5th order Chebychev Lowpass filters:\nUpper path: 1050 MHz cutoff\nLower path: 3000 MHz cutoff"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 270.256 24.892 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "76978f2c-4983-4300-985a-b5230cd04fda")
	)
	(text "Using P and terminating M, looses 3dB but easy \ndiff to single ended, recommended by datasheet"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.83 178.816 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
			)
